\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A nonreal stored link after inversion}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Use two axes of period #{4}, labeled space and time, and
the scalar unitary group #{\{1,\ui,-1,-\ui\}}. Mark the
positive spatial edge from #{(0,1)} by #{\ui}, and take
all other positive links equal to one. Under \ref{fdip-019F}
the marked positive link is now based at #{(3,3)} with value
#{-\ui}. The forward shift coefficient there is its inverse,
#{\ui}. This connection has moved, and its kernel determinant
is equal to the old one for every choice of the real mass
and Wilson coefficient in that result.}

\p{With trivial links, zero mass and zero Wilson coefficient,
the centered kernel contains every constant spin field because its
two shifts agree on constants in each direction. Thus the
determinant equality in the same formula also includes a
vanishing determinant.}
